 "chunks": [
  {
   "text": "In 1859, Bernhard Riemann made the move that changed everything:",
   "start": 0.725,
   "end": 5.338
  },
  {
   "text": "let s be a complex number.",
   "start": 5.338,
   "end": 7.325
  },
  {
   "text": "If you've worked with phasors, you know what that does.",
   "start": 7.325,
   "end": 10.4
  },
  {
   "text": "Write s as σ + it.",
   "start": 10.4,
   "end": 12.612
  },
  {
   "text": "Then n⁻ˢ is an arrow of length n^−σ,",
   "start": 12.612,
   "end": 16.688
  },
  {
   "text": "turned by an angle of t·ln n.",
   "start": 16.688,
   "end": 19.55
  },
  {
   "text": "So zeta is a sum of spinning, shrinking arrows.",
   "start": 20.625,
   "end": 23.8
  },
  {
   "text": "Laid tip to tail, they form a spiral.",
   "start": 23.8,
   "end": 26.5
  },
  {
   "text": "When sigma is bigger than one,",
   "start": 26.5,
   "end": 28.425
  },
  {
   "text": "the arrows shrink fast enough for the spiral to wind into a single point:",
   "start": 28.425,
   "end": 32.675
  },
  {
   "text": "the value of zeta.",
   "start": 32.675,
   "end": 34.125
  }
 ],
